  {
    "episode_id": 91655,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91655.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, so the rural green partnership was a policy that I wrote out of our office, and it was our way of saying, hey, we in the center part of the country, we who are family farmers, we want to make sure that we have a voice as we set policy on climate. And so we focused on things like cover crops on ethanol, biofuels, things like that that play into agriculture and also play into climate. So that was part of the document that I wrote. I testified in front of a select committee on the climate crisis and they have adopted some of our rural green partnership components into the final document. Frankly, if we want to talk politics a little bit, we have been able to pass some policies out of the House that we have not been successful at getting through the Senate. I'm hoping that in 2022, since we're in this new year now, that as we move forward, we'll have some more success of getting good policy through the Senate, so we're able to send that over to the President to be signed into law.",
