    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "that could be, you could take the Head Start program that has been in existence for, gosh, I think actually since the 1960s, I mean, depending on different communities, it came in different places, but the Head Start initially started in the 1960s. But that's the idea is that you give kids, so to speak, a Head Start. That Head Start is The way that's defined and has been built has been for lower income and at-risk families. Universal Pre-K would be for, if you have a three-year-old or you have a four-year-old, that will, under the legislation, that would now be part of public education. And so obviously if we, let's say that passes, that's not going to be in effect in 2022. It's likely to take two plus years to get that implemented as part of public education. So that would be the difference between Head Start, but that would be a model for what could be universal pre-kindergarten.",
